From f06eec40c4fa04295e45ef55c99644ff0f712698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ramin <lordrasmus@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:35:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] loongarch64: no _init and _fini labels in the empty crti

crti.S put the labels _init and _fini into an .init and a .fini section
that stay empty, as crtn.S says they should.  But a defined _init makes
the linker emit DT_INIT, and with nothing in .init the label sits at
whatever comes next, which is the PLT: in tst-tlsmod1.so DT_INIT is
0x7b0, the start of .plt.  The loader calls it at startup or on dlopen,
runs the lazy resolver stub with garbage in its registers and jumps to
-4.  tst-tls3, tst-tls10/11/12/14, tst-tls-at-ctor, dlafk and test3 died
that way, with ra in ld-uClibc.

Leave crti.S empty, like the riscv crtn.S and glibc's empty crti.
Modules linked against it carry no DT_INIT, and those tests pass under
qemu.  libc.so keeps its own DT_INIT, __uClibc_init from -init.

Libraries already linked with the old crti.o, libgcc_s.so.1 of the
current toolchain among them, still carry the bad DT_INIT, so
__UCLIBC_SKIP_DT_INIT__ stays until they are relinked.

Signed-off-by: Ramin Moussavi <lordrasmus@gmail.com>
---
 libc/sysdeps/linux/loongarch64/crti.S | 20 +++++---------------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libc/sysdeps/linux/loongarch64/crti.S b/libc/sysdeps/linux/loongarch64/crti.S
index 64d9aef15..08d5b32cf 100644
--- a/libc/sysdeps/linux/loongarch64/crti.S
+++ b/libc/sysdeps/linux/loongarch64/crti.S
@@ -1,16 +1,6 @@
-/* dummy _init and _fini */
+/* Dummy crti file.
 
-	.section .init
-	.globl	_init
-	.align	2
-	.type	_init,@function
-
-_init:
-
-
-	.section .fini
-	.global	_fini
-	.align	2
-	.type	_fini,@function
-
-_fini: 
\ No newline at end of file
+   In this configuration, crti.o and crtn.o are both empty because the
+   .init_array/.fini_array sections are used exclusively.  No _init or
+   _fini either: a label in an empty .init gets DT_INIT pointed at
+   whatever the linker places next, the PLT.  */
-- 
2.53.0

